I had problems starting nethack with X11R5. It said 

Xlib:  connection to "tellus.csc.fi:0.0" refused by server
Xlib:  Client is not authorized to connect to Server
Error: Can't Open display

even though my other X-programs started OK. The problem was that nethack
is running setuid games so it (meaning Xt toolkit in this case) can't
read my ~/.Xauthority file (protection 0600). The hack I made is to
change to real uid before opening the X connection and back after
that:


*** win/X11/winX.c.orig	Fri Jan 29 14:03:37 1993
--- win/X11/winX.c	Fri Jan 29 14:31:59 1993
***************
*** 778,783 ****
--- 778,786 ----
      static const char *av[] = { "nethack" };
      register const char **pp;
      int i;
+ #ifdef SECURE
+     int uid;
+ #endif
      Cardinal num_args;
      Arg args[4];
  
***************
*** 790,795 ****
--- 793,803 ----
      i = 1;
      num_args = 0;
      XtSetArg(args[num_args], XtNallowShellResize, True);	num_args++;
+ #ifdef SECURE
+     uid=geteuid();
+     seteuid(getuid());
+ # endif
+ 
      toplevel = XtAppInitialize(
  		    &app_context,
  		    "NetHack",		/* application class */
***************
*** 799,804 ****
--- 807,815 ----
  		    args, num_args);
  
      /* We don't need to realize the top level widget. */
+ #ifdef SECURE
+     seteuid(uid);
+ #endif
  
  #ifdef TEXTCOLOR
      /* add new color converter to deal with overused colormaps */


A better fix would be to change to real uid in the main program and
use games (or whatever uid) only while creating/opening files that
need to be protected from the normal users.

